1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,250
- [boy exclaiming]
- [dog barking]

2
00:00:16,916 --> 00:00:20,083
- [growls, exclaims]
- [dog whimpering]

3
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:23,582
- [exclaiming]
- [dog barking, whimpering]

4
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:24,583
[woman] Chun-ting!

5
00:00:25,666 --> 00:00:26,665
You stop that!

6
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:28,332
- [sobbing] Please, don't!
- [woman] Huh?

7
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:30,165
- You shut your mouth!
- [sobs]

8
00:00:30,166 --> 00:00:32,791
Be quiet! I'm sick of hearing you cry.

9
00:00:33,375 --> 00:00:35,916
- Honey, come here.
- [man] What is going on in here?

10
00:00:36,416 --> 00:00:37,957
[woman] Do you know
what your son was doing?

11
00:00:37,958 --> 00:00:39,624
He was torturing Maomao.

12
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:42,457
I told you I wanna get out of here,
you keep stalling!

13
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:44,125
[young Chun-ting whimpers]

14
00:00:44,958 --> 00:00:45,915
- [dad] Damn it!
- [exclaims]

15
00:00:45,916 --> 00:00:47,874
I'm telling you, apologize to your mom.

16
00:00:47,875 --> 00:00:49,832
Hey! He's not mine.

17
00:00:49,833 --> 00:00:52,249
He's someone else's kid,
yours and your ex-wife's.

18
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:53,832
- I don't want to be his mom.
- [whimpering]

19
00:00:53,833 --> 00:00:55,207
[dad] All right, all right.

20
00:00:55,208 --> 00:00:57,082
Calm down. Hey.

21
00:00:57,083 --> 00:00:58,457
[softly] It's all right, isn't it?

22
00:00:58,458 --> 00:01:00,290
Who's a good boy, huh?

23
00:01:00,291 --> 00:01:02,624
- [stepmom] Hello.
- [dad] You're such a good boy.

24
00:01:02,625 --> 00:01:05,916
- [stepmom giggles]
- [breathing heavily]

25
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:08,625
[breath trembling]

26
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:15,250
[opening theme music playing]

27
00:01:42,291 --> 00:01:43,499
MIRACLES OF THE ER

28
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,083
EPISODE 8: THE RELENTLESS

29
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:49,166
[chuckles]

30
00:01:49,666 --> 00:01:51,875
- Hey, good boy.
- [dog pants, whimpers]

31
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:53,500
[chuckles]

32
00:01:54,416 --> 00:01:55,291
[Pi-tan groans]

33
00:01:55,791 --> 00:01:56,791
Oh, sorry, sorry.

34
00:01:57,666 --> 00:01:59,332
- [Pi-tan exclaims]
- [dog barking]

35
00:01:59,333 --> 00:02:01,041
BETEL NUT

36
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:10,583
- [dog continues barking]
- Hey, sir, you want to buy anything?

37
00:02:12,166 --> 00:02:14,082
[dad, softly] It's all right, isn't it?

38
00:02:14,083 --> 00:02:15,499
You shut your mouth!

39
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,166
I'm sick of hearing you cry.

40
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:19,499
- Damn it!
- [exclaims]

41
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,083
[woman] Hey, handsome.
You sure I can't get you anything?

42
00:02:22,666 --> 00:02:24,333
[Chun-ting] Stop barking.
Do you wanna die?

43
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:28,540
- [woman screaming]
- [dog whimpering]

44
00:02:28,541 --> 00:02:30,582
- [woman sobbing]
- [exclaiming]

45
00:02:30,583 --> 00:02:32,916
[woman crying]

46
00:02:33,708 --> 00:02:35,708
[ominous music playing]

47
00:02:39,541 --> 00:02:40,957
Please don't hurt me!

48
00:02:40,958 --> 00:02:42,290
Be quiet!

49
00:02:42,291 --> 00:02:44,250
- I'm sick of hearing you cry.
- [woman sobbing]

50
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:48,124
- [Pi-tan grunts]
- [Chun-ting groans]

51
00:02:48,125 --> 00:02:50,457
- Miss, are you okay?
- [cries]

52
00:02:50,458 --> 00:02:52,374
[Pi-tan] What are you doing?
Put down the knife!

53
00:02:52,375 --> 00:02:53,375
[groans]

54
00:02:54,166 --> 00:02:55,165
[exclaims]

55
00:02:55,166 --> 00:02:56,999
[groans]

56
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,416
- [Chun-ting yells]
- [Pi-tan grunts]

57
00:02:58,916 --> 00:03:00,749
[tense music playing]

58
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:02,583
[both grunt, groan]

59
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:08,083
[Pi-tan grunting]

60
00:03:10,166 --> 00:03:11,665
[screams]

61
00:03:11,666 --> 00:03:13,333
[woman sobbing]

62
00:03:16,791 --> 00:03:18,333
- [Chun-ting yells]
- [Pi-tan groans]

63
00:03:20,666 --> 00:03:22,333
[choking]

64
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,916
[grunts, coughs]

65
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,458
[Pi-tan] What the hell are you doing?
You're crazy!

66
00:03:35,125 --> 00:03:38,249
Oh, what is wrong with you
causing trouble?

67
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:40,499
Didn't your parents
teach you better than that?

68
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,499
- Hey!
- I'm gonna give you a lesson!

69
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,999
- You-- [loud grunt]
- [Geng-ming] Pi-tan!

70
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,583
[Pi-tan] Fuck you, you little brat.

71
00:03:46,166 --> 00:03:48,625
- [grunts]
- Beating up a kid, you crazy?

72
00:03:51,333 --> 00:03:52,165
[Pi-tan] No.

73
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:53,374
No, listen to me.

74
00:03:53,375 --> 00:03:54,749
I saw him with a knife,

75
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:56,624
- trying to rob that girl.
- [yells]

76
00:03:56,625 --> 00:03:58,665
Huh? [exclaims] Watch out!

77
00:03:58,666 --> 00:04:00,250
[woman screams]

78
00:04:08,875 --> 00:04:12,041
[groans]

79
00:04:13,583 --> 00:04:15,832
- [snickers]
- [flesh squelches]

80
00:04:15,833 --> 00:04:17,457
[loud groan]

81
00:04:17,458 --> 00:04:18,707
- [knife shwings]
- [Pi-tan grunts]

82
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:19,790
[Geng-ming] Pi-tan!

83
00:04:19,791 --> 00:04:22,916
- [laughs maniacally]
- [Geng-ming] Pi-tan!

84
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,124
Pi-tan.

85
00:04:25,125 --> 00:04:27,416
- Okay, wait. Slowly. Wait.
- [Pi-tan groaning]

86
00:04:34,708 --> 00:04:37,291
[loud groan]

87
00:04:38,041 --> 00:04:39,541
[Pi-tan] Buddy, are you okay?

88
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:42,124
[grunts] You're the best doctor.

89
00:04:42,125 --> 00:04:44,540
- You better not get hurt.
- You're going to be absolutely fine.

90
00:04:44,541 --> 00:04:45,957
Do you have a first aid kit?

91
00:04:45,958 --> 00:04:47,999
Yeah. Yes, just a second.

92
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,332
I went to pay some bills I owed today.

93
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:52,832
Try not to talk, okay?

94
00:04:52,833 --> 00:04:55,790
- I'm so happy. [groans]
- [footsteps approaching]

95
00:04:55,791 --> 00:04:57,375
- Call an ambulance and the police.
- Okay.

96
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,000
- [Geng-ming sighs]
- [screams in pain]

97
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:02,416
[Geng-ming] Come on.

98
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:07,249
Now my wife isn't gonna get to see me
find another job.

99
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:10,749
I want to show her
that I'm getting it together.

100
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:13,415
No, no, no.
Don't worry, you're gonna be okay.

101
00:05:13,416 --> 00:05:15,624
[groaning]

102
00:05:15,625 --> 00:05:17,708
[somber music playing]

103
00:05:18,916 --> 00:05:20,291
[Geng-ming grunts]

104
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:23,458
[Pi-tan] Thank you...

105
00:05:24,541 --> 00:05:25,375
buddy.

106
00:05:26,625 --> 00:05:29,250
It's a powerful thing, kindness.

107
00:05:31,583 --> 00:05:33,790
- [sighs wearily]
- Pi-tan! Pi-tan!

108
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,875
[bus beeping]

109
00:05:44,416 --> 00:05:45,957
- [woman] Bye, bye.
- [man] Bye.

110
00:05:45,958 --> 00:05:48,499
- [woman] Mmm. See you tomorrow.
- Yeah, see you then.

111
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,582
- Love you.
- [woman] Okay.

112
00:05:49,583 --> 00:05:50,625
[both] Bye!

113
00:05:52,291 --> 00:05:54,791
- You're blocking the door. Step inside.
- [digital beeps]

114
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:56,207
[bus driver] Well?

115
00:05:56,208 --> 00:05:58,207
[echoing] Tap your card
if you want to get on the bus.

116
00:05:58,208 --> 00:06:00,124
Where's your card, stupid? Huh?

117
00:06:00,125 --> 00:06:01,999
You'll get another beating.

118
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,207
Do you wanna die? You're pathetic!

119
00:06:04,208 --> 00:06:05,582
Do you think anyone loves you?

120
00:06:05,583 --> 00:06:07,707
Nobody loves you.

121
00:06:07,708 --> 00:06:09,582
- [bus driver] Make up your mind.
- [breath trembles]

122
00:06:09,583 --> 00:06:11,540
- [grunts]
- [exclaims, gasps]

123
00:06:11,541 --> 00:06:13,958
[laughs maniacally]

124
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:15,874
[gasping]

125
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:17,333
[groans, yelps]

126
00:06:19,416 --> 00:06:22,165
[Chun-ting chuckles]
Let's see who's pathetic.

127
00:06:22,166 --> 00:06:24,916
[suspenseful music playing]

128
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:27,333
You all deserve to die.

129
00:06:28,208 --> 00:06:29,708
[woman giggles] Bye.

130
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:36,833
I-chun! Behind you, I-chun!

131
00:06:37,416 --> 00:06:39,374
- [I-chun screams]
- [passenger] Oh my god!

132
00:06:39,375 --> 00:06:40,749
- [passengers clamoring]
- [groans]

133
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:41,957
No, I-chun!

134
00:06:41,958 --> 00:06:42,999
[huffs]

135
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,957
[clamoring continues]

136
00:06:45,958 --> 00:06:48,082
- [Geng-ming] Over here.
- [siren wailing]

137
00:06:48,083 --> 00:06:50,541
- [EMT 1] BP is 75. Heart rate, 130.
- [Geng-ming] Right.

138
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:59,207
- [sighs]
- [bus driver] Please, help me.

139
00:06:59,208 --> 00:07:00,291
[light thud]

140
00:07:02,125 --> 00:07:03,707
- [gasps]
- [EMT 1] There's another one.

141
00:07:03,708 --> 00:07:04,624
- Notify dispatch.
- Here.

142
00:07:04,625 --> 00:07:05,749
- [EMT 2] Okay.
- First aid kit!

143
00:07:05,750 --> 00:07:07,165
- [EMT 1] Coming!
- Let me take a look.

144
00:07:07,166 --> 00:07:08,875
- [groaning]
- Some gauze.

145
00:07:10,458 --> 00:07:11,832
- [woman] Help!
- [man] Somebody help!

146
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:13,582
[EMT 1] Doctor, over there.

147
00:07:13,583 --> 00:07:15,249
- Please. Over here!
- We need help. Over here!

148
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:16,415
- [man] Here!
- Press on this.

149
00:07:16,416 --> 00:07:18,040
- [woman] Doctor!
- Take these two to Yang-Da.

150
00:07:18,041 --> 00:07:19,875
- And send more ambulances.
- [EMT 2] Yep, got it.

151
00:07:21,583 --> 00:07:24,124
Everyone, let's thank Dr. Chou
for his time today.

152
00:07:24,125 --> 00:07:25,207
Thank you.

153
00:07:25,208 --> 00:07:26,749
[man over PA] <i>Rescue. Move out, 91.</i>

154
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:29,082
<i>Mingxing Park,
large number of injured people.</i>

155
00:07:29,083 --> 00:07:30,874
<i>Unit 91, move out.</i>

156
00:07:30,875 --> 00:07:33,165
- Hey there. I'll come along with you.
- [EMT] Okay.

157
00:07:33,166 --> 00:07:34,540
[alarm ringing]

158
00:07:34,541 --> 00:07:36,749
- What happened here?
- [woman 1] There's a killer on the bus.

159
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:38,665
- Someone tried to stop him...
- Please come with me.

160
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:41,124
Please help her. There's so much blood.
I can't wake her up.

161
00:07:41,125 --> 00:07:42,499
[tense music playing]

162
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,958
[Geng-ming] Miss! Miss!

163
00:07:45,458 --> 00:07:48,207
- [man 1] Are you okay?
- [man 2] We need help over here, please.

164
00:07:48,208 --> 00:07:49,415
[Geng-ming] Here, press on it.

165
00:07:49,416 --> 00:07:51,415
- [man 2 groans]
- [woman 2] Is she gonna be okay?

166
00:07:51,416 --> 00:07:53,832
- [woman 3] I'm bleeding.
- [woman 4] There's a doctor here!

167
00:07:53,833 --> 00:07:56,290
- Come this way. Over here!
- [groans]

168
00:07:56,291 --> 00:07:57,832
[mumbles] What's going on?

169
00:07:57,833 --> 00:08:00,415
- [man 3] Help me. Help me.
- Hang on a sec.

170
00:08:00,416 --> 00:08:02,457
- Wait a minute. Just a...
- [indistinct chatter]

171
00:08:02,458 --> 00:08:04,790
[siren wailing]

172
00:08:04,791 --> 00:08:05,915
[man 1] An ambulance!

173
00:08:05,916 --> 00:08:08,040
- Here! Hurry, please. Over here!
- [woman 2] Help!

174
00:08:08,041 --> 00:08:09,165
Dr. Chou?

175
00:08:09,166 --> 00:08:10,832
- [man 2] Over here.
- [woman 2] Over here!

176
00:08:10,833 --> 00:08:13,540
- Da-bing, get the other injured people.
- [Da-bing] Okay.

177
00:08:13,541 --> 00:08:15,749
- Anyone injured, follow me.
- This man needs some help.

178
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:17,082
What's the situation?

179
00:08:17,083 --> 00:08:19,624
She had no pulse when I got here.
Abdominal wound.

180
00:08:19,625 --> 00:08:22,540
- Multiple CPR rounds, still no pulse.
- [Cheng-chun] Chih-kai.

181
00:08:22,541 --> 00:08:24,958
Go back there and help Da-bing.
People need oxygen.

182
00:08:25,541 --> 00:08:27,374
- [Chih-kai] Here, firm pressure.
- [breath trembling]

183
00:08:27,375 --> 00:08:31,040
I need you to squeeze the bag twice,
on my command.

184
00:08:31,041 --> 00:08:33,041
- First press.
- [man] First.

185
00:08:33,791 --> 00:08:35,249
- [Geng-ming] Second press.
- [man] Second.

186
00:08:35,250 --> 00:08:36,333
Okay.

187
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:38,750
Please save her, doctor.

188
00:08:39,291 --> 00:08:40,499
She just agreed to marry me.

189
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,583
[machine beeping rapidly]

190
00:08:43,291 --> 00:08:45,207
- [machine alarms]
- [Geng-ming pants]

191
00:08:45,208 --> 00:08:46,124
I got no pulse.

192
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:47,082
Keep it going.

193
00:08:47,083 --> 00:08:48,082
[machine beeping rapidly]

194
00:08:48,083 --> 00:08:49,875
Could the liver be damaged
because of the angle?

195
00:08:52,166 --> 00:08:54,415
[tense music continues playing]

196
00:08:54,416 --> 00:08:56,040
[Geng-ming panting]

197
00:08:56,041 --> 00:08:57,957
Wait a sec. What's going on?

198
00:08:57,958 --> 00:09:00,333
We're stopping the bleeding,
otherwise she'll die.

199
00:09:01,083 --> 00:09:03,250
Because it's...
it's your whole hand in there.

200
00:09:04,416 --> 00:09:06,958
Can't you just send her
to the hospital? Please.

201
00:09:10,916 --> 00:09:13,625
I wanna do a Pringle.
I can't go in with the ribs down.

202
00:09:15,083 --> 00:09:17,415
Ready? And stop...

203
00:09:17,416 --> 00:09:19,000
- Now.
- [machine alarms]

204
00:09:20,458 --> 00:09:23,500
TEMPORARILY BLOCKS
LIVER BLOOD FLOW TO REDUCE BLEEDING

205
00:09:24,416 --> 00:09:25,415
[exhales]

206
00:09:25,416 --> 00:09:27,500
[suspenseful music playing]

207
00:09:35,583 --> 00:09:36,499
I got the Pringle.

208
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:37,499
Compressions.

209
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,458
- [panting]
- [hopeful music playing]

210
00:09:42,208 --> 00:09:43,457
Check the pulse.

211
00:09:43,458 --> 00:09:45,165
[machine beeping stabilizes]

212
00:09:45,166 --> 00:09:46,500
[Geng-ming] Look, ROSC.

213
00:09:47,791 --> 00:09:48,790
I got a pulse.

214
00:09:48,791 --> 00:09:50,541
You got a pulse. I-chun...

215
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,540
- [sobs] I-chun.
- [Cheng-chun] Geng-ming.

216
00:09:53,541 --> 00:09:54,957
I can't release the Pringle.

217
00:09:54,958 --> 00:09:57,165
You'll have to stay here.
I'll go with the patient.

218
00:09:57,166 --> 00:09:59,040
You'll be on your own. You can do it.

219
00:09:59,041 --> 00:10:00,124
No.

220
00:10:00,125 --> 00:10:01,750
What about if I can't?

221
00:10:02,875 --> 00:10:03,875
You can.

222
00:10:04,375 --> 00:10:05,375
Because I chose you.

223
00:10:06,416 --> 00:10:07,415
[gentle music playing]

224
00:10:07,416 --> 00:10:09,666
See you there, Dr. Lin.

225
00:10:15,291 --> 00:10:16,708
So you can improve or leave.

226
00:10:18,125 --> 00:10:19,416
Tell me what you decide.

227
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:23,875
<i>Our job is to save lives,
but not just the ones that come to ER.</i>

228
00:10:26,708 --> 00:10:28,500
<i>Not many people would have done that.</i>

229
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,666
<i>This hospital needs a doctor like you.</i>

230
00:10:36,375 --> 00:10:37,374
[Geng-ming] <i>I'll get better.</i>

231
00:10:37,375 --> 00:10:39,500
<i>I want to be an emergency physician.</i>

232
00:10:44,208 --> 00:10:46,165
[music intensifies]

233
00:10:46,166 --> 00:10:47,250
[Geng-ming sighs]

234
00:10:48,541 --> 00:10:50,624
- [injured patients groaning]
- Uh...

235
00:10:50,625 --> 00:10:52,540
[Chih-kai]
I'm sorry, doctor, there's too many.

236
00:10:52,541 --> 00:10:54,124
- We can't treat them all.
- Any extra help?

237
00:10:54,125 --> 00:10:55,625
[Chih-kai] They're still on their way.

238
00:10:56,208 --> 00:10:57,290
Da-bing...

239
00:10:57,291 --> 00:11:00,540
I used to be a nurse,
if you need me to help you.

240
00:11:00,541 --> 00:11:01,625
Miss...

241
00:11:02,625 --> 00:11:05,332
if you can help me triage
and then do basic first aid,

242
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:07,165
then you two, come and assist.

243
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:08,582
And call me if there's an emergency.

244
00:11:08,583 --> 00:11:10,041
- That okay?
- [Da-bing and nurse] Okay.

245
00:11:11,583 --> 00:11:13,624
- Hi, I'm Dr. Lin.
- [woman] Hello, doctor.

246
00:11:13,625 --> 00:11:15,708
Okay, let's help you with that.
Just a second.

247
00:11:18,041 --> 00:11:19,915
[nurse] Doctor, this one's urgent!

248
00:11:19,916 --> 00:11:21,207
- [man groaning]
- Where are we at?

249
00:11:21,208 --> 00:11:22,625
Femoral artery.

250
00:11:23,583 --> 00:11:24,832
[Geng-ming] Press down hard.

251
00:11:24,833 --> 00:11:26,707
I'm going to use a tourniquet
to stop the bleeding.

252
00:11:26,708 --> 00:11:28,249
It's going to hurt a little.

253
00:11:28,250 --> 00:11:30,415
[man exclaiming]

254
00:11:30,416 --> 00:11:31,916
- [loud groan]
- Hold on, okay?

255
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:36,624
[nurse] The bleeding stopped.

256
00:11:36,625 --> 00:11:38,000
[groaning]

257
00:11:39,458 --> 00:11:41,790
- [Geng-ming] Here, help me press on it.
- [woman sobbing]

258
00:11:41,791 --> 00:11:42,832
You're okay.

259
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:45,916
If we can get him to wait over there,
the ambulance can get through.

260
00:11:46,958 --> 00:11:48,249
Okay, next.

261
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:49,457
I'll leave this one to you.

262
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:50,625
[EMT] Got it, doctor.

263
00:11:53,458 --> 00:11:54,749
- [sighs in relief]
- [radio beeps]

264
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:57,083
[dispatcher over radio]
<i>Unit 91, Unit 91. Please respond.</i>

265
00:11:57,666 --> 00:11:59,082
- [radio beeps]
- [Chih-kai] Unit 91 here.

266
00:11:59,083 --> 00:12:00,957
[dispatcher]
<i>We got an injury at a traffic incident</i>

267
00:12:00,958 --> 00:12:02,999
<i>on the corner
of Wenjiasan and Maolin Road.</i>

268
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,874
[Chih-kai] Sorry, we can't attend.
We're still loading patients here. Over.

269
00:12:05,875 --> 00:12:08,707
- [dispatcher] <i>Copy that.</i>
- That's not far from here. Two minutes.

270
00:12:08,708 --> 00:12:09,625
I can be there.

271
00:12:10,250 --> 00:12:12,125
- [Chih-kai] All right. Thank you, Dr. Lin.
- Okay.

272
00:12:14,833 --> 00:12:16,457
Tung-yen, did you see my message?

273
00:12:16,458 --> 00:12:18,582
How's Pi-tan going?
Respond to me if you get this.

274
00:12:18,583 --> 00:12:20,207
[siren wailing]

275
00:12:20,208 --> 00:12:22,457
[tense music playing]

276
00:12:22,458 --> 00:12:23,582
[Chao-i] Trauma Blue.

277
00:12:23,583 --> 00:12:25,790
Dr. He, knife wound to the neck,
significant blood loss.

278
00:12:25,791 --> 00:12:27,332
- [Yu-hua] Resus Room 2.
- [nurse] Got it.

279
00:12:27,333 --> 00:12:28,624
What have we got?

280
00:12:28,625 --> 00:12:30,457
[EMT] Knife wound,
four entry points, abdomen.

281
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:32,332
A doctor on the scene
stemmed the bleeding.

282
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:33,415
Okay, Resus 3.

283
00:12:33,416 --> 00:12:34,707
We'll prep him for surgery,

284
00:12:34,708 --> 00:12:35,708
- inform the OR.
- Uh-huh.

285
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,790
Hsiang-chun, what's up?

286
00:12:38,791 --> 00:12:41,040
Pi-tan got stabbed. He's bleeding badly.

287
00:12:41,041 --> 00:12:42,915
Did anyone come in with him?

288
00:12:42,916 --> 00:12:45,124
I didn't see anyone. I gotta go.

289
00:12:45,125 --> 00:12:48,082
Sir, you're in the hospital now.
Everything's going to be all right.

290
00:12:48,083 --> 00:12:49,540
- [Hsiang-chun] Be still.
- [loud groan]

291
00:12:49,541 --> 00:12:51,415
[Yu-hua] Draw blood for cross-match.

292
00:12:51,416 --> 00:12:52,332
It's all right now.

293
00:12:52,333 --> 00:12:54,624
- [Hsiang-chun] Hang in there.
- [Yu-hua] Pi-tan, it's okay,

294
00:12:54,625 --> 00:12:55,624
Stay still.

295
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:57,040
It hurts.

296
00:12:57,041 --> 00:12:58,332
Hsiang-chun, ketorolac.

297
00:12:58,333 --> 00:13:00,415
[Pi-tan] It hurts so much. [loud groan]

298
00:13:00,416 --> 00:13:01,332
Calm down.

299
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:03,915
- [Yu-hua] Hold on, sir.
- Calm down. Hold on.

300
00:13:03,916 --> 00:13:04,957
It won't be long.

301
00:13:04,958 --> 00:13:07,540
[tense music continues playing]

302
00:13:07,541 --> 00:13:08,749
MISSED CALL

303
00:13:08,750 --> 00:13:10,832
[Geng-ming]
<i>Tung-yen, Pi-tan's on his way there.</i>

304
00:13:10,833 --> 00:13:13,499
<i>Remember, he's allergic to ketorolac.
Don't administer.</i>

305
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,457
Wait, stop!

306
00:13:14,458 --> 00:13:15,707
[Yu-hua] Press on it, hurry!

307
00:13:15,708 --> 00:13:17,540
- [loud groan]
- Okay, get it into him.

308
00:13:17,541 --> 00:13:18,665
Hold on, sir.

309
00:13:18,666 --> 00:13:20,291
- [Wen-chih] Deep breath.
- [Tung-yen] Wait!

310
00:13:22,125 --> 00:13:23,332
The patient's allergic.

311
00:13:23,333 --> 00:13:24,915
He'll go into anaphylactic shock.

312
00:13:24,916 --> 00:13:26,165
[Pi-tan groans]

313
00:13:26,166 --> 00:13:27,125
[Hsiang-chun gasps]

314
00:13:28,958 --> 00:13:30,416
[sighs wearily]

315
00:13:33,875 --> 00:13:34,957
[man] Hello, emergency?

316
00:13:34,958 --> 00:13:36,666
When will the ambulance arrive?

317
00:13:38,833 --> 00:13:39,833
[Geng-ming] Sir, sir.

318
00:13:40,375 --> 00:13:41,915
What happened here? I'm a doctor.

319
00:13:41,916 --> 00:13:44,540
Well, he's got cyanosis.
Altered consciousness.

320
00:13:44,541 --> 00:13:46,957
GCS E1 V1 M4.

321
00:13:46,958 --> 00:13:47,957
Respiratory trouble.

322
00:13:47,958 --> 00:13:49,875
And judging from this,
he's got a femur fracture.

323
00:13:50,875 --> 00:13:52,000
So you're an MD?

324
00:13:57,291 --> 00:13:58,291
[muted groans]

325
00:13:58,875 --> 00:14:00,166
Right has decreased breath sounds.

326
00:14:00,791 --> 00:14:02,499
Tympanic percussion.
Chest asymmetric expansion.

327
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,499
- Tension pneumothorax.
- He needs needle decompression.

328
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,666
[Geng-ming] Right.

329
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:09,665
I thought you were the doctor.

330
00:14:09,666 --> 00:14:10,749
Oh, okay.

331
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:11,833
[breathing heavily]

332
00:14:13,041 --> 00:14:14,875
[suspenseful music playing]

333
00:14:20,916 --> 00:14:22,166
[flesh squelches]

334
00:14:24,166 --> 00:14:26,332
- [tense music playing]
- [air hisses]

335
00:14:26,333 --> 00:14:29,791
[gasps, exhales]

336
00:14:35,375 --> 00:14:36,750
[Geng-ming] Hey, thank you.

337
00:14:37,916 --> 00:14:39,000
How did you get here?

338
00:14:39,583 --> 00:14:41,457
I ran over here
from a major trauma incident.

339
00:14:41,458 --> 00:14:44,458
I was the only doctor there,
and I came here when I heard about it.

340
00:14:45,083 --> 00:14:46,458
You sure that was a good idea?

341
00:14:47,041 --> 00:14:48,624
You left other injured patients

342
00:14:48,625 --> 00:14:50,708
to come and save someone
whose condition you didn't know.

343
00:14:51,583 --> 00:14:53,457
- Emotions got to you.
- [siren wailing]

344
00:14:53,458 --> 00:14:54,791
I...

345
00:14:58,375 --> 00:15:00,000
[motorcycle revs]

346
00:15:03,375 --> 00:15:05,790
[reporter on TV] <i>Reporting live
from the scene of mass casualties,</i>

347
00:15:05,791 --> 00:15:07,499
<i>where there have been
multiple people stabbed.</i>

348
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:10,375
<i>The suspect is a teenager
previously accused of animal cruelty.</i>

349
00:15:10,958 --> 00:15:12,540
Hey, Tung-yen!

350
00:15:12,541 --> 00:15:14,665
Did you get my messages?
He can't have ketorolac.

351
00:15:14,666 --> 00:15:16,790
Hey, chill. We didn't give it to him.

352
00:15:16,791 --> 00:15:17,999
[Yu-hua] Dr. Lin.

353
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,374
Pi-tan's stable now.

354
00:15:19,375 --> 00:15:21,415
You handled his first aid well.

355
00:15:21,416 --> 00:15:24,083
We're taking him to the OR.
I'll brief them myself.

356
00:15:24,875 --> 00:15:26,291
- Well done.
- [panting] Yeah.

357
00:15:27,041 --> 00:15:28,041
Thank you, doctor.

358
00:15:31,375 --> 00:15:34,083
- [ominous music playing]
- [siren wailing]

359
00:15:37,250 --> 00:15:38,832
[policeman 1] All teams, take positions.

360
00:15:38,833 --> 00:15:40,749
[policeman 2 over megaphone]
<i>You're surrounded.</i>

361
00:15:40,750 --> 00:15:42,874
<i>Drop your weapon and surrender now.</i>

362
00:15:42,875 --> 00:15:44,958
[cell phone vibrating]

363
00:15:45,958 --> 00:15:46,958
[groans]

364
00:15:49,416 --> 00:15:50,416
[grunts]

365
00:15:52,958 --> 00:15:53,958
[gasps]

366
00:16:01,708 --> 00:16:04,832
[old woman over phone] <i>My boy.
Why weren't you home for dinner?</i>

367
00:16:04,833 --> 00:16:06,124
- Grandma.
- [grandma] <i>Huh?</i>

368
00:16:06,125 --> 00:16:07,707
[somber music playing]

369
00:16:07,708 --> 00:16:09,166
<i>Have you eaten yet?</i>

370
00:16:11,250 --> 00:16:13,916
- But, Grandma, what have I done?
- [grandma] <i>What?</i>

371
00:16:14,625 --> 00:16:15,750
<i>What are you saying?</i>

372
00:16:17,458 --> 00:16:18,458
<i>What happened?</i>

373
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:21,499
<i>- Where are you?
-</i> [Chun-ting sobs]

374
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:24,041
[grandma]
<i>Chun-ting, sweetheart? Chun-ting.</i>

375
00:16:26,458 --> 00:16:27,833
Grandma, I'm sorry.

376
00:16:36,333 --> 00:16:37,541
[policeman 3] Put down the knife.

377
00:16:38,125 --> 00:16:39,125
[policeman 4] Freeze!

378
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,166
[policeman 3] Call an ambulance.

379
00:16:50,916 --> 00:16:52,416
[mumbles] Coming home now.

380
00:16:54,833 --> 00:16:56,624
I'm... coming home.

381
00:16:56,625 --> 00:16:58,541
[siren wailing]

382
00:17:00,333 --> 00:17:01,541
[Chia-hsin] Okay, got it.

383
00:17:02,041 --> 00:17:03,040
Dr. Cheng.

384
00:17:03,041 --> 00:17:04,707
[sighs] Cheng-chun, where have you been?

385
00:17:04,708 --> 00:17:06,125
I was in the OR. What's up?

386
00:17:06,625 --> 00:17:07,624
[Chia-hsin] Gentlemen.

387
00:17:07,625 --> 00:17:09,749
Since Yang-Da is the closest hospital

388
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:12,875
and because our security
can handle any disruption,

389
00:17:13,875 --> 00:17:15,250
they've decided to send...

390
00:17:15,791 --> 00:17:17,208
the suspect to us.

391
00:17:17,958 --> 00:17:19,833
- [Shao-ching sighs]
- [Chia-hsin] They're almost here.

392
00:17:21,875 --> 00:17:24,125
EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT

393
00:17:34,250 --> 00:17:35,458
Please remove his cuffs.

394
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:45,582
- [Cheng-chun] Let's get him inside.
- [EMT] Okay.

395
00:17:45,583 --> 00:17:47,750
[slow tense music playing]

396
00:17:50,166 --> 00:17:51,416
[Hsiu-ju] Tourniquet done.

397
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:55,957
- [Cheng-chun] His vitals?
- [Su-ching] Heart rate, 153.

398
00:17:55,958 --> 00:17:57,082
BP can't be detected.

399
00:17:57,083 --> 00:17:59,040
Hsiu-ju, can I get an IV?

400
00:17:59,041 --> 00:18:00,540
Normal saline challenge.

401
00:18:00,541 --> 00:18:02,624
- Four units of whole blood, O neg.
- [Hsiu-ju] Okay.

402
00:18:02,625 --> 00:18:04,999
- Consult cardiovascular. Contact OR.
- Right.

403
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,958
Okay. The echo.

404
00:18:09,666 --> 00:18:12,332
[machine beeping]

405
00:18:12,333 --> 00:18:15,708
[Su-ching] This is Resus Room 1.
Patient needs emergency surgery.

406
00:18:20,416 --> 00:18:21,416
[sighs heavily]

407
00:18:22,833 --> 00:18:25,957
Right side pleural effusion.
32 French tube.

408
00:18:25,958 --> 00:18:27,082
We'll do drainage first.

409
00:18:27,083 --> 00:18:28,874
We have to stabilize him
before we operate.

410
00:18:28,875 --> 00:18:29,791
Right.

411
00:18:32,250 --> 00:18:34,290
Are you okay? You don't need to be here.

412
00:18:34,291 --> 00:18:35,416
Mmm-hmm.

413
00:18:36,708 --> 00:18:37,707
Are we ready?

414
00:18:37,708 --> 00:18:38,791
Scalpel.

415
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:45,333
Kelly.

416
00:18:53,375 --> 00:18:54,208
Chest tube.

417
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,708
[flesh squelches]

418
00:19:00,291 --> 00:19:01,500
[Cheng-chun] Clamp.

419
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,500
[burbling]

420
00:19:14,291 --> 00:19:15,333
It's working.

421
00:19:16,541 --> 00:19:18,458
- [Cheng-chun] Vitals are stable.
- Blood's here.

422
00:19:19,416 --> 00:19:22,332
- [Cheng-chun] Is the OR ready?
- Yeah. But the patient is a minor.

423
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:24,582
- We'll need a signed consent form.
- Well, where's his family?

424
00:19:24,583 --> 00:19:27,124
We informed his grandma.
I guess she'll be here in a minute.

425
00:19:27,125 --> 00:19:29,207
But there's protesters
inside the hospital.

426
00:19:29,208 --> 00:19:32,041
- He'll be in danger if he stays here.
- [Cheng-chun] Got it.

427
00:19:33,791 --> 00:19:36,290
[reporter on TV] <i>Footage taken
this evening appears to show the suspect</i>

428
00:19:36,291 --> 00:19:39,332
<i>stabbing multiple people
at a food stall and local park.</i>

429
00:19:39,333 --> 00:19:40,915
<i>During a standoff with police,</i>

430
00:19:40,916 --> 00:19:43,207
<i>he is reported to have
turned the knife on himself.</i>

431
00:19:43,208 --> 00:19:44,624
<i>Now in a critical condition,</i>

432
00:19:44,625 --> 00:19:46,790
<i>the suspect has been taken
to a local hospital.</i>

433
00:19:46,791 --> 00:19:48,791
[nurse] I heard
he was brought here to Yang-Da.

434
00:19:49,625 --> 00:19:50,624
[groans]

435
00:19:50,625 --> 00:19:53,665
- [nurse] What are you doing?
- Help me. Can you get my clothes?

436
00:19:53,666 --> 00:19:55,207
- They're over there.
- [nurse] Okay.

437
00:19:55,208 --> 00:19:57,291
[indistinct chatter]

438
00:19:58,291 --> 00:19:59,665
[reporter on TV] <i>The teenage suspect</i>

439
00:19:59,666 --> 00:20:02,207
<i>was abandoned by his parents
in elementary school...</i>

440
00:20:02,208 --> 00:20:03,915
- [man 1] That's her.
- [man 2] What a disgrace.

441
00:20:03,916 --> 00:20:06,290
Hey! Look, that's the killer's grandma.

442
00:20:06,291 --> 00:20:08,457
[people clamoring]

443
00:20:08,458 --> 00:20:10,999
<i>...has turned this boy into a problem.</i>

444
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,957
<i>We learned from the neighbors
that he enjoys torturing animals.</i>

445
00:20:14,958 --> 00:20:17,083
[indistinct chatter]

446
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,915
- [man 1] Shame on you.
- [woman] You raised a monster.

447
00:20:19,916 --> 00:20:22,083
[people clamoring]

448
00:20:26,375 --> 00:20:27,832
- Ma'am, hi.
- [sobbing]

449
00:20:27,833 --> 00:20:29,165
[man 1] Locked away for good.

450
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:31,415
Doctor, where is Chun-ting?

451
00:20:31,416 --> 00:20:32,499
Is he okay?

452
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:34,999
- I'll take you there.
- [woman] What are you gonna do?

453
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,124
[overlapping shouting]

454
00:20:38,125 --> 00:20:39,291
[Hsi, loudly] That's enough!

455
00:20:39,833 --> 00:20:41,457
- This is a hospital.
- [whimpers]

456
00:20:41,458 --> 00:20:42,957
[Hsi] Whatever happened outside,

457
00:20:42,958 --> 00:20:45,125
we're still trying to care
for patients here.

458
00:20:46,125 --> 00:20:48,791
And it's not fair
you're all aggressive and angry.

459
00:20:49,833 --> 00:20:51,583
Please give everyone some space.

460
00:20:52,375 --> 00:20:54,291
- [sobs]
- [Hsi] Come with me, please.

461
00:21:02,291 --> 00:21:04,082
Um, madam, here's the thing.

462
00:21:04,083 --> 00:21:06,749
Your grandson's bleeding internally.
We need to operate.

463
00:21:06,750 --> 00:21:08,791
Can you sign this consent form, please?

464
00:21:09,458 --> 00:21:10,458
[grandma] Oh...

465
00:21:14,666 --> 00:21:16,125
[breathing heavily]

466
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:25,250
Maybe...

467
00:21:26,541 --> 00:21:29,165
he will not survive.

468
00:21:29,166 --> 00:21:30,375
Would that be...

469
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:32,458
a good thing?

470
00:21:33,833 --> 00:21:35,833
[somber music playing]

471
00:21:37,333 --> 00:21:38,916
[grandma breath trembles]

472
00:21:40,875 --> 00:21:41,875
Uh...

473
00:21:44,458 --> 00:21:45,958
It's all my fault.

474
00:21:49,541 --> 00:21:52,791
I made mistakes bringing up your father.

475
00:21:53,708 --> 00:21:56,083
I made mistakes with you as well.

476
00:21:57,625 --> 00:21:59,375
Why can't you see?

477
00:22:00,541 --> 00:22:04,041
That you are so adored, so loved.

478
00:22:05,416 --> 00:22:07,333
It's all my fault.

479
00:22:11,208 --> 00:22:13,625
I failed you, my boy.

480
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:16,416
[sobbing]

481
00:22:23,083 --> 00:22:25,790
[reporter] <i>Just now, a large group
of protesters at Yang-Da's ER</i>

482
00:22:25,791 --> 00:22:27,415
<i>are blocking the entrance.</i>

483
00:22:27,416 --> 00:22:29,124
<i>It is reported
that we will have a statement</i>

484
00:22:29,125 --> 00:22:30,624
<i>from the hospital shortly.</i>

485
00:22:30,625 --> 00:22:32,500
[people clamoring]

486
00:22:34,041 --> 00:22:36,082
As Yang-Da is at critical capacity,

487
00:22:36,083 --> 00:22:38,290
we can't provide treatment
for all patients.

488
00:22:38,291 --> 00:22:41,124
We'll transfer critical cases
to another hospital.

489
00:22:41,125 --> 00:22:44,374
And, yes, we'll hold a press conference
to answer other questions.

490
00:22:44,375 --> 00:22:45,915
Thank you. We appreciate it.

491
00:22:45,916 --> 00:22:48,125
[clamoring]

492
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,415
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

493
00:22:50,416 --> 00:22:52,916
[man 1] Hey, he's coming out.
He's coming out!

494
00:22:55,208 --> 00:22:57,499
- [man 2] Get him out of there!
- Let us through, please.

495
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:58,583
Excuse me.

496
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:00,999
Make way, please.

497
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,458
[policeman 1] Back away now.

498
00:23:02,958 --> 00:23:04,332
Step back.

499
00:23:04,333 --> 00:23:07,290
[policeman 2] Get back, please. Stay back.

500
00:23:07,291 --> 00:23:09,665
[policeman 1] Make way. Step back.

501
00:23:09,666 --> 00:23:12,082
- [reporter] Can we have any...
- [policeman 1] Back up!

502
00:23:12,083 --> 00:23:13,625
[reporter] Why did he do this?

503
00:23:15,083 --> 00:23:17,582
EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT

504
00:23:17,583 --> 00:23:19,540
- [siren wailing]
- Is this going to help?

505
00:23:19,541 --> 00:23:21,625
[slow tense music plays]

506
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:31,750
[EMT] All clear.

507
00:23:32,791 --> 00:23:34,665
- [grunts]
- [music fades]

508
00:23:34,666 --> 00:23:36,583
[sighs] Ma'am, you okay?

509
00:23:40,208 --> 00:23:42,625
[grandma]
Chun-ting wasn't like this before.

510
00:23:43,416 --> 00:23:45,291
When he first came to live with me,

511
00:23:46,458 --> 00:23:48,040
he'd come into the garden,

512
00:23:48,041 --> 00:23:50,791
and he'd say, "Hug me, Grandma."

513
00:23:51,375 --> 00:23:53,416
He was so cute in those days.

514
00:23:54,166 --> 00:23:56,166
Then he went to live with his father.

515
00:23:57,041 --> 00:23:59,291
He was so different when he came back.

516
00:23:59,875 --> 00:24:03,708
I don't know what happened.
He was so changed after that.

517
00:24:05,833 --> 00:24:07,040
And now,

518
00:24:07,041 --> 00:24:10,416
they're shouting scum at us out there.

519
00:24:11,125 --> 00:24:13,875
They told him he belongs in hell.

520
00:24:14,375 --> 00:24:15,707
[sobs]

521
00:24:15,708 --> 00:24:16,791
Ma'am.

522
00:24:17,916 --> 00:24:19,540
Chun-ting is your only grandson.

523
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:21,124
[melancholic music playing]

524
00:24:21,125 --> 00:24:24,458
You can't let others tell you
whether he deserves to live or not.

525
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:28,041
[breathes heavily, whimpers]

526
00:24:32,125 --> 00:24:33,125
Take this.

527
00:24:33,833 --> 00:24:34,833
Trust me.

528
00:24:42,625 --> 00:24:45,375
SIGNATURE OF CONSENTING PARTY

529
00:24:47,208 --> 00:24:48,958
- Dr. Chou, we have consent.
- [Cheng-chun] Okay.

530
00:24:50,291 --> 00:24:51,791
Guys, he's all yours.

531
00:24:52,458 --> 00:24:54,291
[doctor] Okay. Prepare to start.

532
00:24:54,791 --> 00:24:57,540
- Anesthesiology, happy?
- [anesthesiologist] Vitals okay.

533
00:24:57,541 --> 00:24:59,415
- [doctor] Okay. Scalpel.
- [nurse] Scalpel.

534
00:24:59,416 --> 00:25:01,500
[calm music playing]

535
00:25:08,416 --> 00:25:10,208
- [doctor] Making incision.
- [nurse] Yep.

536
00:25:15,541 --> 00:25:18,125
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

537
00:25:21,208 --> 00:25:22,166
[Geng-ming sighs]

538
00:25:23,125 --> 00:25:24,375
[nurse] He's doing really well.

539
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,915
He should be out of bed in a few days.

540
00:25:26,916 --> 00:25:28,458
Okay. Thank you, nurse.

541
00:25:30,791 --> 00:25:32,500
When you're awake, I can thank you.

542
00:25:34,375 --> 00:25:35,458
Thank you for saving me...

543
00:25:36,708 --> 00:25:37,708
buddy.

544
00:25:38,208 --> 00:25:40,208
[gentle music playing]

545
00:25:46,375 --> 00:25:47,457
How's your stomach?

546
00:25:47,458 --> 00:25:48,541
Okay, I guess.

547
00:25:49,083 --> 00:25:50,083
You weren't stabbed?

548
00:25:50,916 --> 00:25:51,916
No.

549
00:25:53,166 --> 00:25:54,500
I was really scared today.

550
00:25:56,458 --> 00:25:57,791
A doctor like me,

551
00:25:58,500 --> 00:26:01,333
out there on my own,
trying to save people,

552
00:26:01,916 --> 00:26:03,083
without you next to me,

553
00:26:04,208 --> 00:26:05,750
and everyone else.

554
00:26:06,625 --> 00:26:07,833
You did a really good thing.

555
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:09,500
Do you mean it?

556
00:26:10,083 --> 00:26:11,082
Of course.

557
00:26:11,083 --> 00:26:13,083
You underestimate yourself, you know.

558
00:26:16,750 --> 00:26:18,750
[both chuckling softly]

559
00:26:23,166 --> 00:26:26,250
[Geng-ming] I promised his grandma
that I'd keep it close to him.

560
00:26:27,750 --> 00:26:30,083
[Hsi] He looks even thinner
than last time.

561
00:26:30,666 --> 00:26:33,415
The news said that
after his father abandoned him,

562
00:26:33,416 --> 00:26:35,582
he did things to get people's attention.

563
00:26:35,583 --> 00:26:38,500
They called him a freak at school.
Bullied him.

564
00:26:39,083 --> 00:26:41,083
[Geng-ming]
Yeah, his grandma told me how much...

565
00:26:42,458 --> 00:26:44,416
he just really wanted to be hugged.

566
00:26:46,208 --> 00:26:47,999
[Hsi] When he came to the ER last time,

567
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:50,000
if I had done more,

568
00:26:51,583 --> 00:26:53,541
could this whole thing
have been prevented?

569
00:26:58,208 --> 00:27:00,040
[Geng-ming]
Let's try and face things together.

570
00:27:00,041 --> 00:27:01,124
From now on.

571
00:27:01,125 --> 00:27:03,208
[gentle music continues playing]

572
00:27:07,583 --> 00:27:09,583
[music fades]

573
00:27:11,625 --> 00:27:12,625
[Chih-cheng] Got a question.

574
00:27:13,500 --> 00:27:14,499
What about?

575
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:17,082
It's been kind of crazy
over the last few days.

576
00:27:17,083 --> 00:27:18,500
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

577
00:27:19,083 --> 00:27:20,040
[Chih-cheng] Hmm.

578
00:27:20,041 --> 00:27:22,040
Curry rice. Mixed.

579
00:27:22,041 --> 00:27:23,915
Eat and don't forget to rest.

580
00:27:23,916 --> 00:27:26,000
[lighthearted music playing]

581
00:27:27,708 --> 00:27:28,707
[Chih-cheng sighs]

582
00:27:28,708 --> 00:27:29,665
What am I saying?

583
00:27:29,666 --> 00:27:31,666
You're strong as a bull.
You don't need me.

584
00:27:32,208 --> 00:27:33,083
[Hsiu-ju] Wait a minute.

585
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:37,208
So I wondered if...

586
00:27:38,333 --> 00:27:39,583
you were injured yesterday.

587
00:27:40,333 --> 00:27:42,457
- No.
- Do I need to check you out?

588
00:27:42,458 --> 00:27:43,540
[Chih-cheng] No, I'm fine.

589
00:27:43,541 --> 00:27:45,625
[playful music playing]

590
00:27:47,458 --> 00:27:49,125
[Hsiu-ju whispers] I need to examine you.

591
00:28:02,291 --> 00:28:03,416
[door locks]

592
00:28:09,291 --> 00:28:11,124
Hey, Cheng-chun.

593
00:28:11,125 --> 00:28:12,500
- [Chia-hsin] Cheng-chun.
- Yu-hua.

594
00:28:15,166 --> 00:28:16,166
[Cheng-chun] Uh, hi there.

595
00:28:16,750 --> 00:28:19,915
We need a surgical update from OR
and other details,

596
00:28:19,916 --> 00:28:21,499
so PR can brief the media.

597
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:23,332
It seems you're going to be busy.

598
00:28:23,333 --> 00:28:27,124
By the way, thanks for taking
Lin Geng-ming's suggestion. The getaway.

599
00:28:27,125 --> 00:28:29,166
I didn't do it for Lin Geng-ming.

600
00:28:31,916 --> 00:28:35,415
Well, let me know
if there's anything I can do to help.

601
00:28:35,416 --> 00:28:36,624
And thanks again.

602
00:28:36,625 --> 00:28:37,707
Anytime.

603
00:28:37,708 --> 00:28:39,125
Will you come see my dad?

604
00:28:42,041 --> 00:28:43,665
[Cheng-chun]
Yu-hua, were you looking for me?

605
00:28:43,666 --> 00:28:46,416
- Mmm, it's nothing. I'll leave you to it.
- [Cheng-chun] Okay.

606
00:28:50,833 --> 00:28:54,625
- Why the 13th floor? Is he with a patient?
- [Chia-hsin] You'll see when we get there.

607
00:28:55,500 --> 00:28:56,458
You know something?

608
00:28:57,125 --> 00:29:00,333
In the race for career or family,

609
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:03,374
my dad chose
what he thought was important.

610
00:29:03,375 --> 00:29:06,915
Everyone is different,
but he always loved this hospital.

611
00:29:06,916 --> 00:29:09,165
My dad worked in Yang-Da his whole life,

612
00:29:09,166 --> 00:29:11,165
and he's used to sacrifices.

613
00:29:11,166 --> 00:29:13,541
He's done everything he can to protect it.

614
00:29:14,125 --> 00:29:15,125
Chia-hsin.

615
00:29:15,625 --> 00:29:16,750
I wanna be clear with you.

616
00:29:17,333 --> 00:29:18,957
Huang You-chang's paper does not add up.

617
00:29:18,958 --> 00:29:20,749
Your father must know this.

618
00:29:20,750 --> 00:29:22,540
This makes it impossible to ignore.

619
00:29:22,541 --> 00:29:26,583
Drug companies and hospitals
are big enough to be independent.

620
00:29:27,166 --> 00:29:29,457
But they can't survive without each other.

621
00:29:29,458 --> 00:29:32,708
And so much of our research
is also Axo funded.

622
00:29:33,208 --> 00:29:35,874
You don't seem to realize
that this is how it is.

623
00:29:35,875 --> 00:29:38,040
How do we fund a hospital
without any money?

624
00:29:38,041 --> 00:29:40,332
- How do we keep saving lives?
- [Cheng-chun sighs heavily]

625
00:29:40,333 --> 00:29:42,416
- [Chia-hsin sighs]
- [pensive music playing]

626
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:46,124
- [Cheng-chun] Chia-hsin.
- [sighs]

627
00:29:46,125 --> 00:29:47,333
Cheng-chun.

628
00:29:49,041 --> 00:29:50,375
Has it occurred to you

629
00:29:51,125 --> 00:29:53,500
that your idea
of how the ER should function

630
00:29:54,416 --> 00:29:55,791
is too naive?

631
00:29:57,666 --> 00:29:59,666
[pensive music continues playing]

632
00:30:09,666 --> 00:30:10,665
Cheng-chun.

633
00:30:10,666 --> 00:30:12,999
How's the hand? Is it better?

634
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:14,625
[chuckles] It's great.

635
00:30:16,833 --> 00:30:19,833
Why do I still feel like
you're that young resident

636
00:30:20,958 --> 00:30:22,333
who just got here?

637
00:30:23,083 --> 00:30:25,208
And doesn't know how to do an intubation.

638
00:30:26,041 --> 00:30:27,041
[chuckles]

639
00:30:27,708 --> 00:30:29,165
That was so long ago.

640
00:30:29,166 --> 00:30:32,875
I still remember that I gave you

641
00:30:33,916 --> 00:30:36,374
- your first stethoscope, right?
- Sure.

642
00:30:36,375 --> 00:30:37,500
[Hsueh-hung chuckles softly]

643
00:30:38,375 --> 00:30:39,833
You're a great doctor now.

644
00:30:40,916 --> 00:30:42,250
You really made it.

645
00:30:42,833 --> 00:30:45,291
You lived up to all my expectations.

646
00:30:47,208 --> 00:30:48,208
Director, what's the matter?

647
00:30:49,750 --> 00:30:52,041
Pancreatic cancer, stage three.

648
00:30:52,708 --> 00:30:55,832
You know I worked hard
to keep this hospital going.

649
00:30:55,833 --> 00:30:58,166
I got funding from everywhere,

650
00:30:59,625 --> 00:31:02,791
just so we could keep saving patients.

651
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:06,375
And do you know what's funny?

652
00:31:07,500 --> 00:31:08,500
[scoffs]

653
00:31:10,375 --> 00:31:12,916
I can't even save myself.

654
00:31:13,666 --> 00:31:17,665
[sighs] Director Chang,
you know we've got the greatest doctors.

655
00:31:17,666 --> 00:31:19,290
You can beat this.

656
00:31:19,291 --> 00:31:20,416
[Hsueh-hung] Cheng-chun.

657
00:31:20,958 --> 00:31:23,041
You know I only have one wish.

658
00:31:24,208 --> 00:31:25,833
But it's not for myself.

659
00:31:26,708 --> 00:31:29,250
It's for my wife and Chia-hsin.

660
00:31:30,250 --> 00:31:31,500
I'm begging you.

661
00:31:32,833 --> 00:31:35,166
Don't publish your research paper

662
00:31:36,375 --> 00:31:39,208
that says the new drug is ineffective.

663
00:31:42,375 --> 00:31:43,625
Can you do that?

664
00:31:53,541 --> 00:31:54,708
How come you're still here?

665
00:31:56,375 --> 00:31:57,208
Ah.

666
00:31:57,708 --> 00:32:00,833
So you were waiting outside the OR
to change my dressing?

667
00:32:02,333 --> 00:32:03,915
Oh, you're smart.

668
00:32:03,916 --> 00:32:05,875
You haven't put it down all day, have you?

669
00:32:06,458 --> 00:32:07,291
[exclaims]

670
00:32:07,875 --> 00:32:09,833
- Did you grow eyes on your back?
- [Cheng-chun chuckles]

671
00:32:10,416 --> 00:32:12,333
[Yu-hua giggles] Sit down.

672
00:32:13,375 --> 00:32:14,749
I just saw the news.

673
00:32:14,750 --> 00:32:17,375
Geng-ming out there
working hard to save those people.

674
00:32:19,250 --> 00:32:20,500
When he returned,

675
00:32:21,125 --> 00:32:22,833
his coat was covered in blood.

676
00:32:25,125 --> 00:32:27,540
Which kind of reminded me of you,

677
00:32:27,541 --> 00:32:30,125
back when you treated
the gas explosion victims.

678
00:32:31,250 --> 00:32:32,333
I thought maybe...

679
00:32:33,625 --> 00:32:34,958
he couldn't treat the killer.

680
00:32:35,666 --> 00:32:36,875
But then he just...

681
00:32:37,375 --> 00:32:39,041
came and helped me with the surgery.

682
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:41,165
- [Yu-hua] Mmm-hmm.
- [scoffs]

683
00:32:41,166 --> 00:32:44,208
I'm not so sure
whether I would have been like him.

684
00:32:44,875 --> 00:32:46,375
Can't choose your patients.

685
00:32:47,833 --> 00:32:49,291
Can't give up on them either.

686
00:32:50,791 --> 00:32:51,750
Well, I think...

687
00:32:52,250 --> 00:32:53,750
he must have learned a lot today.

688
00:32:54,583 --> 00:32:57,374
And I hope
this bottom-of-the-pack doctor you chose

689
00:32:57,375 --> 00:32:59,457
keeps sticking to his values.

690
00:32:59,458 --> 00:33:01,541
[gentle music playing]

691
00:33:06,416 --> 00:33:07,500
What do you keep looking at?

692
00:33:09,291 --> 00:33:11,249
I'm just wondering
if all of your lecturing

693
00:33:11,250 --> 00:33:14,250
is designed to remind me
to stick to my paper?

694
00:33:15,416 --> 00:33:16,916
I'm glad to see that your...

695
00:33:17,666 --> 00:33:19,583
hand is all healed, and you're okay.

696
00:33:22,958 --> 00:33:24,958
[music fades]

697
00:33:33,750 --> 00:33:34,749
[Cheng-chun] <i>Director Chang,</i>

698
00:33:34,750 --> 00:33:39,250
is Axo's drug as effective
as Huang You-chang says it is?

699
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:44,541
The answer is...

700
00:33:45,041 --> 00:33:46,041
foggy.

701
00:33:49,791 --> 00:33:51,040
I remember when...

702
00:33:51,041 --> 00:33:52,915
[pensive music playing]

703
00:33:52,916 --> 00:33:55,500
...you led us all
reciting the Hippocratic Oath.

704
00:33:56,125 --> 00:33:58,415
To consider dear to me as my parents,

705
00:33:58,416 --> 00:33:59,833
he who taught me this art.

706
00:34:03,125 --> 00:34:04,541
It wasn't always easy.

707
00:34:05,958 --> 00:34:07,291
But I try to live by that.

708
00:34:08,291 --> 00:34:10,332
And as I sit here today,

709
00:34:10,333 --> 00:34:12,208
the respect I had for you...

710
00:34:16,083 --> 00:34:17,125
is gone now.

711
00:34:19,375 --> 00:34:21,624
[pensive music continues playing]

712
00:34:21,625 --> 00:34:22,708
[breathes heavily]

713
00:34:27,916 --> 00:34:29,040
SEND

714
00:34:29,041 --> 00:34:31,125
[pensive music turns tense]

715
00:34:37,666 --> 00:34:39,666
UPLOADING. DO NOT CLOSE

716
00:34:44,250 --> 00:34:45,665
UPLOAD COMPLETE

717
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:47,290
[music fades]

718
00:34:47,291 --> 00:34:49,833
[Hsueh-hung] Did you see the paper
Cheng-chun submitted?

719
00:34:50,458 --> 00:34:53,207
[Chia-hsin] We're well-acquainted with
one of the journal's committee members.

720
00:34:53,208 --> 00:34:55,583
We've already obtained
some internal information.

721
00:34:56,166 --> 00:34:58,665
We're working up a plan
to handle the media.

722
00:34:58,666 --> 00:35:00,375
Axo, goddamn it...

723
00:35:01,416 --> 00:35:03,499
- could potentially have seen it.
- [Chia-hsin] Yes.

724
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:05,041
They called first thing this morning.

725
00:35:07,458 --> 00:35:09,041
I'll check the stock price again.

726
00:35:10,333 --> 00:35:11,500
Aside from the company,

727
00:35:12,083 --> 00:35:15,458
the clinical trial patients
and their families will be unhappy.

728
00:35:16,041 --> 00:35:17,832
Huang You-chang says it works.

729
00:35:17,833 --> 00:35:19,541
Chao Cheng-chun says it doesn't.

730
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:22,833
They're going to ask us about it
at the press conference.

731
00:35:24,958 --> 00:35:26,750
I doubt they'd know about it yet.

732
00:35:28,125 --> 00:35:31,250
Just talk about the stabbings
and see what happens, okay?

733
00:35:32,708 --> 00:35:33,875
And the paper...,

734
00:35:34,750 --> 00:35:36,083
I'll figure something out.

735
00:35:41,291 --> 00:35:43,291
[pensive music playing]

736
00:35:44,458 --> 00:35:46,375
[butler] Chairman, Director Chang.

737
00:35:46,958 --> 00:35:47,916
Good to see you, sir.

738
00:35:48,791 --> 00:35:50,000
[Chang-kuo] Regarding the paper...

739
00:35:50,958 --> 00:35:53,625
Do whatever it takes
to stop it from being published.

740
00:35:54,583 --> 00:35:55,583
If you have to,

741
00:35:56,250 --> 00:35:57,375
get rid of Chou Cheng-chun.

742
00:36:00,750 --> 00:36:02,166
[Hsueh-hung] Yes, chairman.

743
00:36:05,708 --> 00:36:06,708
[man] Dad.

744
00:36:07,291 --> 00:36:08,291
I'm home.

745
00:36:23,708 --> 00:36:25,708
[music fades]

746
00:36:26,791 --> 00:36:30,832
Oh! You're the guy from the accident, huh?
I didn't catch your name.

747
00:36:30,833 --> 00:36:32,999
Are you consulting here or...

748
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:34,166
Can I be of any help?

749
00:36:34,875 --> 00:36:37,833
Well, you sure can't help
with what I need.

750
00:36:40,125 --> 00:36:42,208
[Geng-ming] I don't think
I let emotions get to me.

751
00:36:42,791 --> 00:36:45,583
Everyone I treated yesterday
got decent care, you know.

752
00:36:46,166 --> 00:36:47,999
And even the most serious cases
are stable.

753
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:51,333
Who, as a doctor, wouldn't try to save
as many people as they can?

754
00:36:52,083 --> 00:36:55,375
- Only if I don't, would I regret it.
- [scoffs]

755
00:36:56,708 --> 00:36:57,708
So, what's your name?

756
00:36:58,833 --> 00:36:59,832
Lin Geng-ming.

757
00:36:59,833 --> 00:37:01,333
ER doctor, R1.

758
00:37:02,875 --> 00:37:03,833
I'll remember you.

759
00:37:08,708 --> 00:37:09,625
[exclaims]

760
00:37:12,875 --> 00:37:14,832
Good morning, everyone, and thank you.

761
00:37:14,833 --> 00:37:18,624
An update on our most critical victim
of the park incident

762
00:37:18,625 --> 00:37:20,040
is that he's stable for now.

763
00:37:20,041 --> 00:37:22,290
I would like to introduce the ER director,

764
00:37:22,291 --> 00:37:26,791
and he can talk about how Yang-Da Hospital
did so well this week.

765
00:37:27,416 --> 00:37:29,124
- [reporter 1] Ms. Chang.
- It's a pleasure to be...

766
00:37:29,125 --> 00:37:32,957
It's been revealed that the doctor
who treated the people in Minxing Park

767
00:37:32,958 --> 00:37:35,624
is Dr. Lin Geng-ming,
from your own emergency department.

768
00:37:35,625 --> 00:37:37,082
- Can we talk to him?
- No.

769
00:37:37,083 --> 00:37:38,165
- Go on.
- I don't know.

770
00:37:38,166 --> 00:37:39,540
Geng-ming, come here.

771
00:37:39,541 --> 00:37:40,999
[chuckles awkwardly]

772
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:42,083
[Geng-ming] Director.

773
00:37:43,458 --> 00:37:45,915
Oh, it's you! Good to see you!

774
00:37:45,916 --> 00:37:48,500
[all chuckle]

775
00:37:49,750 --> 00:37:53,375
Dr. Lin, can you tell us all
about what you faced yesterday?

776
00:37:54,333 --> 00:37:55,750
Well, I just wanted to help.

777
00:37:56,333 --> 00:37:59,207
[reporter 1] In this tragedy,
it's a miracle that at this time,

778
00:37:59,208 --> 00:38:01,207
every single injured person survived.

779
00:38:01,208 --> 00:38:03,125
Is that because of the great job you did?

780
00:38:03,750 --> 00:38:06,040
[hesitates]
I wouldn't really put it like that.

781
00:38:06,041 --> 00:38:08,374
It was thanks to the help
of people around me

782
00:38:08,375 --> 00:38:10,249
that so many are okay.

783
00:38:10,250 --> 00:38:12,124
[gentle music playing]

784
00:38:12,125 --> 00:38:14,416
I just did what a doctor does.

785
00:38:16,083 --> 00:38:17,541
I do want to thank somebody.

786
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:21,125
Dr. Chou Cheng-chun.

787
00:38:23,333 --> 00:38:24,833
He never gave up on me.

788
00:38:25,708 --> 00:38:27,833
And he's the reason that I'm a doctor.

789
00:38:28,875 --> 00:38:29,707
Thank you so much.

790
00:38:29,708 --> 00:38:32,000
[all applauding, cheering]

791
00:38:38,958 --> 00:38:40,958
[music fades]

792
00:38:43,500 --> 00:38:46,540
That's the chairman
of the hospital's eldest son.

793
00:38:46,541 --> 00:38:49,124
[reporter 2] Wasn't he abroad?
Why is he back?

794
00:38:49,125 --> 00:38:51,207
[reporter 3]
Mr. Yen, you've been practicing overseas.

795
00:38:51,208 --> 00:38:52,625
Why the return to Taiwan?

796
00:38:53,166 --> 00:38:54,082
Everyone, hello.

797
00:38:54,083 --> 00:38:56,374
The star of the show today
is the emergency department.

798
00:38:56,375 --> 00:38:58,957
Dr. Lin, you did a great job there.

799
00:38:58,958 --> 00:39:00,958
- Well done.
- Oh...

800
00:39:01,750 --> 00:39:02,750
When did he get back?

801
00:39:03,250 --> 00:39:06,832
I'd like to bring the focus
back to Dr. Lin Geng-ming today.

802
00:39:06,833 --> 00:39:08,624
And so, what if he's a new resident?

803
00:39:08,625 --> 00:39:10,790
Under our training here,

804
00:39:10,791 --> 00:39:13,582
his response under pressure
was impressive.

805
00:39:13,583 --> 00:39:16,958
Is your return this time anything to do
with the management of the hospital?

806
00:39:17,708 --> 00:39:20,790
All I can say
is how much I'm looking forward

807
00:39:20,791 --> 00:39:23,040
to assisting with the restructure
of the hospital.

808
00:39:23,041 --> 00:39:24,790
To make it an international hub,

809
00:39:24,791 --> 00:39:27,208
and soon the announcements
for that are coming.

810
00:39:28,041 --> 00:39:29,041
Thanks, everyone.

811
00:39:31,541 --> 00:39:33,165
[tense music builds]

812
00:39:33,166 --> 00:39:34,457
Dr. Chou, good to see you.

813
00:39:34,458 --> 00:39:36,625
The paper you're about to publish
is very interesting.

814
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:38,208
I've heard a lot about it.

815
00:39:40,500 --> 00:39:41,582
Welcome back.

816
00:39:41,583 --> 00:39:43,582
[camera shutter clicking]

817
00:39:43,583 --> 00:39:45,500
[tense music turns dramatic]

818
00:39:50,791 --> 00:39:51,790
[music swells]

819
00:39:51,791 --> 00:39:53,875
[music fades]

820
00:39:55,583 --> 00:39:57,583
[dramatic music playing]
